* Problems in Multithreading code.

I) Race Condition : 
  Jo Bhi Hamara Program hoga uska jo final state hoga woh depend karega ki konsa thread phele execute
  ho rahi thi , kitne context switching ho rahi thi un sab condition par depend karega
- It Will depend on the order of execution of threads.

example : 
int cnt = 0;
cnt++;

so ye increment operation ek atomic operation nahi hain, atomic operations means jisko hum further 
operations main divide nahi kar sakte hain.

cnt++ operation can be divide into three operation : 
i) Read value of cnt from Memory(RAM) and store into its registor.
ii) Increment the value of cnt by 1 in its registor. 
iii) we will write the updated value back into the Again Memory (RAM) from its registor value.

But if we use Multithreading then there is Race Condition problem bw two running threads so result depend
on the order of execution of cnt++ inner operation.
ya Ye order of execution depend karega ki ye jo 3 operations hain woh kaise threads execute kar rahe hain
or means ye jo multhithread hain woh in 3 operation ko kis order main execute kar rahe hain.

Jaise ki 
Thread t1,t2 ek sath run ho rahi hain , means ye dono ya toh parallely run ho rahi hain ya context 
switching karke run ho rahi hain or concurrently run ho rahi hain so op non-deterministic hain.

Race condition scenario : 
Ho sakta hain ki thread t1,t2 simultaneously chale jaye cnt++ karne
possible condition of order of execution of the value of cnt by two threads -> for one core cpu

steps      t1               t2 
1       read c = 0          -                   // not running -> (-)
2         -                 read c = 0          // Yaha ho gayi context switching t1 to t2
3      c=0 -> c=1             -               // Again CS (Context Swithcing)
4        -                  c=0 -> c = 1       // Again CS
5   write c =1 in RAM          -                // Agian cs
6       -                    write c=1 in RAM    // Again cs

so Jaise ki 2 thread run kar rahe hian , toh cnt ki value ko 0 se 2 jana chaiye. but ja rahe hain 
sirf 1 kyuki t2 ne phir se cnt ki value ko 1 se overwrite kar diya hain. so this is called race 
condition

Chahe ye parralley bhi chale toh ye dono thread ek value of cnt ko same le leneg in its registor for 
its calcualtion so it is also a race condition.

* Critical Section : 
 Ye woh area hota hain hamare program ka jo Multiplethreads apas main share kar rahe hain. and woh
risky area hain. because cnt variable is used by both 
threads so there is high chance that two threads can go inisde cnt at same time or both thread used 
this variable value at same time. and then race condition happens
// So that type of area or variable we need to protect from Race Condition is called Critical section.
// Shared Resources -> cnt++
// Crtical section -> class method which do cnt++ like increment function() who is doing cnt++

so Shared resources woh sare chije ho sakte hain jo sari critical section ke andar lie kar rahe ho
void increment() {
cn++;
}
* Increment function -> critical section because it is used by both threads to increment the values of cnt
* all variable inside the Increment function methods are a shared resourcres. like cnt


